Dear Participant,

Congratulations on successfully completing 14 weeks of lectures in Cohort=
=20
10! [image: =F0=9F=8E=89] Welcome to Week 15 of TRI AI Saturdays Cohort 10!=
 [image:=20
=F0=9F=9A=80] With the lecture phase now complete, the next step is to focu=
s on=20
finalising your team project and preparing for the project evaluation and=
=20
Demo Day.
Please take note of the key dates and submission requirements below. Key=20
Date [image: Screenshot 2026-09-06 at 20.01.12.png]
1. Development Phase
  =20
   -=20
  =20
   Wednesday, 9 September: Competition development phase closes.
   -=20
  =20
   9=E2=80=9312 September: Projects will be evaluated on an unseen test dat=
aset.=20
   This dataset was not available during the development phase.
  =20
2. Final Project Submission =E2=80=94 12 September

By 12 September, each team must submit one GitHub repository link=20
containing the complete project and all four Cohort Challenges.
Your project must be submitted as a public GitHub repository containing the=
=20
following:
  =20
   1.=20
  =20
   README.md =E2=80=94 maximum 6,000 characters (references excluded), cove=
ring:
   -=20
     =20
      Dataset: Describe the data you used and how it was selected or=20
      created.
      -=20
     =20
      Training Pipeline: Describe data collection, preprocessing,=20
      hyperparameter search, and key model/design choices.
      -=20
     =20
      Evaluation: Explain how you tested and verified your method.
      -=20
     =20
      Reproduction: Provide clear instructions on which scripts to run and=
=20
      in what order.
      - Appendix: Include a list of contributors/team members and mentors.
   2.=20
  =20
   Code
   -=20
     =20
      Include all code required to reproduce your results from scratch.
      3.=20
  =20
   Data
   -=20
     =20
      Include the dataset if size and licensing allow. Otherwise, provide=
=20
      scripts or instructions for automatically downloading or loading the =
data.
     =20
Submission Form:
The GitHub repository link must be submitted by 12 September to allow us to=
 complete=20
the evaluation and select the top teams.
Form for Submission: https://forms.gle/2Vx1iyn2hdcUZR7dA  Teams can use the=
=20
following repository as an example:
https://github.com/AISaturdaysLagos/C9-team-nwapa
3. Repository Structure The repository should contain all required project=
=20
materials and follow a clear, organised structure. For example: 4. All 4=20
Cohort Challenges All 4 Cohort Challenges must be included in the GitHub=20
repository. These challenges were completed throughout the different=20
modules, starting with =E2=80=9CDevelop Your Problem Statement=E2=80=9D in =
Course 1.The=20
docs/ folder must contain:
  =20
   1. Problem Statement =E2=80=93 problem_statement.pdf
   2. Data Card =E2=80=93 data_card.pdf
   3. Impact Statement Card =E2=80=93 impact_statement_card.pdf
   4. Stakeholder Engagement =E2=80=93 stakeholder_engagement.pdf
  =20
  =20
5. Project Code & Scripts
  =20
   - Include all project scripts and relevant code in the GitHub repository=
.
   - The code should be clearly organised, for example in a scripts/ or src=
/=20
   folder.
   - The code submitted to GitHub must match the final submission made on=
=20
   Kaggle/CodaBench.
   - Please ensure that the repository contains all relevant files needed=
=20
   to understand the project and reproduce the final submission.=20

6. What Happens After the Final Submission?After the final submission:
  =20
   - 16 September: Top teams will be selected and notified.
   - 26 September: Selected teams will submit their presentation slides.
   - 27 September =E2=80=93 2 October: Selected teams will practise their d=
emos=20
   with their mentors.
   - 3 October: Demo Day.=20

You can find the complete project requirements and details here:=20
https://aisaturdayslagos.github.io/cohort_structure/cohort10/projects.html

Thank you for your consistency and commitment throughout the course. As you=
=20
move into the final stage, stay focused, work closely with your team, and=
=20
finish strong. We look forward to seeing what you=E2=80=99ve built.

TRI AI Programme Team
cohorts@tri-ai.org

